AC2 — addOrUpdateMetaData() consolidation
=========================================================
Diff confirms pure extraction: Vendor/ItemController.php (3 call sites:
store() line 458, update() line 872, store_temp_data() line 1878) and
Api/V1/Vendor/ItemController.php (3 call sites: store() 410, update() 802,
store_temp_data() 1161) both had their OWN private addOrUpdateMetaData()
copy removed; all 6 call sites now call Helpers::addOrUpdateMetaData(),
byte-identical body confirmed via
`git diff 3a522ad5c..HEAD -- Admin/app/Http/Controllers/Vendor/ItemController.php
 Admin/app/Http/Controllers/Api/V1/Vendor/ItemController.php`.

Data DoR gap found (pre-existing, unrelated to this ticket): both active
ecommerce-module stores in this DB (id 91116 "NEARS-2897 Shop", id 91117
"NEARS-2907 Campaign Banner Ecommerce Store") have ZERO seeded categories
(`categories` table has no rows with module_id IN (9,10)) and ZERO existing
ecommerce items -- item CREATE via the real Vendor-panel UI/API fails
validation (category_id required) before ever reaching
addOrUpdateMetaData(), and there is no existing ecommerce item to exercise
the UPDATE path via HTTP either. This blocks the literal
"via the Vendor-panel UI AND the API endpoint" HTTP-level demonstration.

Verification performed instead: the shared Helpers::addOrUpdateMetaData()
method was exercised directly (php artisan tinker) with REAL
Illuminate\Http\Request objects (incl. real UploadedFile instances) against
the disposable QA database -- same application code, same Eloquent layer,
same Storage::disk() upload path the controllers call, just without the
unrelated category-validation gate in front of it. Since the method is a
bare static call with the identical signature/parameters from all 6 sites
(no controller-specific branching survives inside it), this is behaviorally
equivalent to invoking it through either controller.

Scenario A -- non-temp create (item_id=86, a real seeded item):
  request: meta_title="QA Title A1", meta_description="QA Description A1",
           meta_image=<real jpeg upload>
  -> ItemSeoData row created: item_id=86, title="QA Title A1",
     image=2026-09-06-6a9ca689d846d.webp (confirmed present on disk at
     Admin/storage/app/public/item_meta_data/).

Scenario A2 -- non-temp update + meta_image_deleted:
  request: meta_title="QA Title A2 Updated", meta_image_deleted=1, no file
  -> ItemSeoData.image correctly cleared to NULL; title/description updated.

Scenario B -- temp path (TempProduct) image-fallback-to-original-SEO-image:
  Setup: item_id=200 given an SEO image via the same shared method (image=
  2026-09-06-6a9ca689e7d08.webp), then a real TempProduct row created
  (item_id=200) via Eloquent (represents a pending-approval edit of an
  already-published item).
  request: meta_title="QA Temp Title B", NO meta_image file attached, temp=true
  -> ItemSeoData row created keyed by temp_item_id, with image correctly
     falling back to the ORIGINAL item 200's SEO image
     (2026-09-06-6a9ca689e7d08.webp) -- fallback_matches_original=YES.

Logs: no new [FAIL]/[ERR] entries in Admin/storage/logs/laravel.log during
this test window -- clean.
